      "text": "To determine the month Hal will change the batteries for the 25th time, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the intervals between battery changes:**\n   - Hal changes the batteries every 5 months.\n\n2. **Calculate the total years and months for the 25th change:**\n   - Since each change occurs 5 months later, the number of years and months can be calculated as follows:\n     - For the \\( n \\)-th change, the number of years is \\( \\left\\lfloor \\frac{n-1}{5} \\right\\rfloor \\) years.\n     - The number of months is \\( 5 \\left( n - \\left\\lfloor \\frac{n-1}{5} \\right\\rfloor \\right) \\) months.\n\n3. **Determine the total number of months for the 25th change:**\n   - For \\( n = 25 \\):\n     \\[\n     \\text{Years} = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{25-1}{5} \\right\\rfloor = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{24}{5} \\right\\rfloor = 4 \\text{ years}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{Months} = 5 \\left( 25 - 4 \\right) = 5 \\times 21 = 105 \\text{ months}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Convert the total months into years and months:**\n   - 105 months is equivalent to:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Years} = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{105}{12} \\right\\rfloor = 8 \\text{ years}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{Remaining months} = 105 - 8 \\times 12 = 105 - 96 = 9 \\text{ months}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Determine the final month:**\n   - The first change was in May. \n   - Adding 8 years and 9 months to May:\n     - Adding 8 years to May results in the following months:\n       \\[\n       \\text{February 2024, March 2024, April 2024, May 2024, June 2024, July 2024, August 2024, September 2024}\n       \\]\n     - Adding 9 months to the last month of the previous year that was a collection month (August 2024):\n       \\[\n       \\text{September 2024, October 2024, November 2024, December 2024, January 2025, February 2025, March 2025, April 2025, May 2025}\n       \\]\n\nThus, the batteries will be changed for the 25th time in \\boxed{\\text{May 2026}}.",
