      "text": "To determine the month in which Hal will change the batteries the 25th time, we start by noting that the batteries are changed every 5 months. We need to find out the total number of months that will have passed after 25 such intervals.\n\nFirst, calculate the total number of months:\n\\[\n25 \\text{ intervals} \\times 5 \\text{ months/interval} = 125 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to convert 125 months into years and months. Since there are 12 months in a year, we divide 125 by 12:\n\\[\n125 \\div 12 = 10 \\text{ years and } 5 \\text{ months}\n\\]\nSo, 125 months is equivalent to 10 years and 5 months.\n\nNow, we need to determine the month after 10 years and 5 months. If we start from May and go forward for 10 years, we will go through the years sequentially:\n\\[\n\\text{Months in a year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\nAfter 10 years, we move to the 11th year and continue counting:\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 11th year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 12th year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 13th year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 14th year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 15th year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 16th year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 17th year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 18th year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 19th year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 20th year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 21st year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 22nd year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 23rd year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 24th year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 25th year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 26th year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 27th year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months in the 28th year} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\nAfter 27 years, we are just entering 28 years. Therefore, the date will be the same in the 28th year as it was in the 27th year, which is the same as the 1st day of the 2nd month of the 28th year.\n\nSince the 1st month is January, we count the 5 months from January:\n\\[\n\\text{Months in January} = 12 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Months from Jan to May} = 5 \\text{ months}\n\\]\nThus, the batteries will be changed in May of the 28th year.\n\nTherefore, the month in which Hal will change the batteries the 25th time is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{May}}\n\\]",
