      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the month when Hal will change the batteries for the 25th time, we need to calculate the time interval between each change and then find the month 25 times this interval from the initial month.\n\n1. **Determine the interval between battery changes:**\n   - Hal changes the batteries every 5 months.\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of intervals for 25 changes:**\n   - Since there are 25 changes, there will be \\(25 - 1 = 24\\) intervals between these changes (because the first change is in May, and each subsequent change is 5 months later).\n\n3. **Calculate the total time in months:**\n   - Each interval is 5 months, so for 24 intervals, the total time is:\n     \\[\n     24 \\times 5 = 120 \\text{ months}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Determine the month 120 months after May:**\n   - To find the month, we need to convert 120 months into years and months.\n   - There are 12 months in a year, so:\n     \\[\n     120 \\div 12 = 10 \\text{ years}\n     \\]\n   - Since 10 years is the same as 0 years and 120 months, we only need to find the month within 120 months.\n   - Adding 120 months to the initial month (May):\n     - 120 months is exactly 10 years, and since there are 12 months in a year, adding 120 months means adding 10 years, which means moving forward 10 years from May.\n     - May + 10 years = May + 1 year = May + 1 = April\n\nSo, the batteries will be changed the 25th time in \\(\\boxed{\\text{April}}\\).",
